  "body": "Following discussion in #10479 (and especially https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/10479#issuecomment-887001086), I've checked the sync response when Synapse does not have OTK (one time key) anymore. So when the number of OTK is changing from N to 0.\r\n\r\nInstead of receiving \r\n\r\n```json\r\n\"device_one_time_keys_count\":{\"signed_curve25519\":0}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe client receives\r\n\r\n```json\r\n\"device_one_time_keys_count\":{}\r\n```\r\n\r\nand so the client cannot distinguish \"no change\" and \"no OTK left\", and do not upload new OTK, which at the end breaks decryption of some messages.\r\n\r\nServer version: 1.38.0 commit 12c92eec1\r\n",
